 "sections": [
  {
   "name": "How a Car Engine Works",
   "lines": [
    [
     "c01_1",
     {
      "label": "hook",
      "head": "Your car runs on *tiny explosions*",
      "pose": "point",
      "face": "grin",
      "prop": {
       "type": "engine4",
       "speed": 2.4
      }
     },
     "Every time you drive, your engine is setting off thousands of tiny explosions every minute."
    ],
    [
     "c01_2",
     {
      "label": "the cylinder",
      "head": "It all happens in a *cylinder*",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "smile",
      "prop": {
       "type": "engine4",
       "speed": 1.2
      }
     },
     "Inside each cylinder, a piston slides up and down. A rod connects it to the crankshaft, which turns that motion into spinning."
    ],
    [
     "c01_3",
     {
      "label": "stroke 1",
      "head": "Stroke one: *intake*",
      "pose": "count",
      "face": "smile",
      "prop": {
       "type": "engine4",
       "stroke": 0
      }
     },
     "Stroke one, intake. The piston moves down, and the intake valve lets in air and fuel."
    ],
    [
     "c01_4",
     {
      "label": "stroke 2",
      "head": "Stroke two: *compression*",
      "pose": "think",
      "face": "think",
      "prop": {
       "type": "engine4",
       "stroke": 1
      }
     },
     "Stroke two, compression. Both valves close, and the piston squeezes the mixture into a tiny space."
    ],
    [
     "c01_5",
     {
      "label": "stroke 3",
      "head": "Stroke three: *power*",
      "pose": "cheer",
      "face": "wow",
      "prop": {
       "type": "engine4",
       "stroke": 2
      }
     },
     "Stroke three, power. The spark plug fires, the mixture burns, and the pressure shoves the piston down. This is what drives the car."
    ],
    [
     "c01_6",
     {
      "label": "stroke 4",
      "head": "Stroke four: *exhaust*",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "smile",
      "prop": {
       "type": "engine4",
       "stroke": 3
      }
     },
     "Stroke four, exhaust. The exhaust valve opens, and the piston pushes the burnt gas out. Then it all starts again."
    ],
    [
     "c01_7",
     {
      "label": "the math",
      "head": "At 3,000 rpm: *1,500* bangs a minute",
      "pose": "count",
      "face": "grin",
      "prop": {
       "type": "stat",
       "from": 0,
       "to": 1500,
       "sub": "POWER STROKES PER MINUTE, PER CYLINDER"
      }
     },
     "Each cylinder fires once every two turns. So at three thousand rpm, that is fifteen hundred power strokes a minute, in every cylinder."
    ],
    [
     "c01_8",
     {
      "label": "remember it",
      "head": "Suck, squeeze, bang, *blow*",
      "pose": "thumbs",
      "face": "happy",
      "prop": {
       "type": "engine4",
       "speed": 3
      }
     },
     "Mechanics remember it as suck, squeeze, bang, blow."
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
